{
  "description": "A handler invocation is a separate, DEFERRED instruction rather than part of the loop that registered it, so a `repcount` whose nearest lexically enclosing `repeat` is outside the handler block raises `ol-repcount-outside-repeat` \"however the loop is placed and whether or not it has finished\" (spec/execution-model.md:682-690). Here the enclosing `repeat` is still running when the handler fires — the `wait` is inside the loop body — so a runtime that simply let the handler body inherit the registering scope's active turn stack would print a turn number instead. A `repeat` written INSIDE a handler block is unaffected and is covered separately by the runtime's unit suite.",
